        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="1015" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg955"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Caracas,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 22, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith, for
                    the information of the department, a communication dated July 7 but received
                    July 18 inclosure No. 1, with the translation of the same, inclosure No. 2,
                    relative to the conduct of General J. M. Aristiguieta, the chief of staff of
                    General Bruzual, before and during the recent siege of Caracas. In inclosure No.
                    3 will be found a copy of the argument between General Aristiguieta and General
                    José T. Monagas, concerning terms of capitulation, &amp;c., and inclosure No. 4
                    contains a translation of the same. * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ERASTUS C. PRUYN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



